-- Tests of the TAS-era instruments deposited on 2026-11-04 from the follow-up list: the Order O 3 (S 549/1998 and the 1999 Revised Edition), Rg 7 (1999 Ed.), the Dealers Regulations, and Rg 3 (1999 Ed.), the Radio-communication Regulations.
-- Every expected value is read from the 1999 Revised Edition copy or from S 549/1998 (the line quoted in the module), not from the L4.

§ `O 3: in operation, within the exemption, and the two readings of section 30 of the TAS Act`
-- S 549/1998 para 1: "shall come into operation on 12th November 1998".
#ASSERT NOT (`O 3 para 1: the Order is in operation on the date (from 12 November 1998; continued by s 98(2) from 1 December 1999; no revoking instrument found)` (Date 11 11 1998))
#ASSERT `O 3 para 1: the Order is in operation on the date (from 12 November 1998; continued by s 98(2) from 1 December 1999; no revoking instrument found)` (Date 12 11 1998)
#ASSERT `O 3 para 1: the Order is in operation on the date (from 12 November 1998; continued by s 98(2) from 1 December 1999; no revoking instrument found)` (Date 4 11 2026)
-- Para 2: limb (a) is approval for sale under reg 24(1) of Rg 7; limb (b) is Fifth Schedule equipment that also meets the published standards.
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is within the exemption` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is within the exemption` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`O 3 para 2: the equipment is within the exemption` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`O 3 para 2: the equipment is within the exemption` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`O 3 para 2: the equipment is within the exemption` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The fork: with the reading of section 30(1) to (5) not supplied the answer is NOTHING; on branch 1 the Order does not reach possession or operation; on branch 2 it exempts exactly the equipment within the exemption.
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` `the text of section 30 is not held` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` `section 30(1) to (5) was the approval-before-use requirement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` `section 30(1) to (5) was the approval-before-use requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` `section 30(1) to (5) was the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` `section 30(1) to (5) was the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` `section 30(1) to (5) was the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` `section 30(1) to (5) was the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the approval-before-use requirement` `the text of section 30 is not held` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the approval-before-use requirement` `section 30(1) to (5) was the approval-before-use requirement` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the approval-before-use requirement` `section 30(1) to (5) was the approval-before-use requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the approval-before-use requirement` `section 30(1) to (5) was the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.): in operation, and the regulations that decide who may sell what`
-- The Telecommunications Act 1999 came into operation on 1 December 1999 (s 3(1)); s 98(2) continues the Regulations; the end day, 1 April 2003, is ASSUMED.
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 26 of S 185/2003, in operation 2 April 2003)` (Date 30 11 1999))
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 26 of S 185/2003, in operation 2 April 2003)` (Date 1 12 1999)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 26 of S 185/2003, in operation 2 April 2003)` (Date 1 4 2003)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 26 of S 185/2003, in operation 2 April 2003)` (Date 2 4 2003))
-- Reg 4(1): no person other than a holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence shall deal in equipment other than type-approved equipment or Fifth Schedule equipment.
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(3): the holder may sell equipment that is not type-approved equipment or not set out in the Fifth Schedule` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(3): the holder may sell equipment that is not type-approved equipment or not set out in the Fifth Schedule` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(3): the holder may sell equipment that is not type-approved equipment or not set out in the Fifth Schedule` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4A(1): the dealer is deemed to have been granted a Dealer's Class Licence for that purpose` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 4A(1): the dealer is deemed to have been granted a Dealer's Class Licence for that purpose` FALSE)
-- Reg 24(1) and (2): approval for sale of line-connected or radio-communication equipment, none needed for Fifth Schedule equipment.
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24(1) and (2): the dealer contravenes the regulation` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24(1) and (2): the dealer contravenes the regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24(1) and (2): the dealer contravenes the regulation` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 24(1) and (2): the dealer contravenes the regulation` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 23: First Schedule equipment may not be manufactured, sold or possessed for sale unless approved; nor equipment that does not meet the published standards.
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 23: the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 23: the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 23: the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 23: the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(1): the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(1): the person contravenes the regulation, despite the grant of a Telecommunication Dealer's Licence` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(2): approval may be granted for the import of the equipment` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(2): approval may be granted for the import of the equipment` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 20(2): approval may be granted for the import of the equipment` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 30: the dealer is meeting the regulation` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 30: the dealer is meeting the regulation` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 30: the dealer is meeting the regulation` FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 13: $400 per annum; $50 for every 5 years; the late fee bands (after 7 days but less than 15: $10; after 14 days but less than 31: $20; after 30 days: $50).
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(1): the fee payable in dollars for the licence` "Dealer's Individual Licence, per annum" EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(1): the fee payable in dollars for the licence` "Dealer's Class Licence, for every 5 years" EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(1): the fee payable in dollars for the licence` "Other" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(3): the late payment fee in dollars` 7 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(3): the late payment fee in dollars` 8 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(3): the late payment fee in dollars` 14 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(3): the late payment fee in dollars` 15 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(3): the late payment fee in dollars` 30 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 13(3): the late payment fee in dollars` 31 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 6(2): the licensee has notified the Authority within the time` 14
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 6(2): the licensee has notified the Authority within the time` 15)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 33: the employee may compound the offence by collecting the sum from a person reasonably suspected of committing it` 1000 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 33: the employee may compound the offence by collecting the sum from a person reasonably suspected of committing it` 1001 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 33: the employee may compound the offence by collecting the sum from a person reasonably suspected of committing it` 1000 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) reg 32: the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE
-- The schedules.
#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule: the equipment is named` "Scanning Receivers"
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 (1999 Ed.) First Schedule: the equipment is named` "Modem")
