#ASSERT `Rg 7 (1999 Ed.): the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date 2 4 2003) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.): in operation, "station", reg 4(1), the First Schedule and the fees`
-- Reg 80(1) of S 114/2001 revokes these Regulations; S 114/2001 is in operation on 2 March 2001, so the last day is 1 March 2001.
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 80(1) of S 114/2001, in operation 2 March 2001)` (Date 30 11 1999))
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 80(1) of S 114/2001, in operation 2 March 2001)` (Date 1 12 1999)
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 80(1) of S 114/2001, in operation 2 March 2001)` (Date 1 3 2001)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date, as continued by s 98(2) (from 1 December 1999 until revoked by reg 80(1) of S 114/2001, in operation 2 March 2001)` (Date 2 3 2001))
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.): the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date 1 12 1999) (Date 1 7 1999) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 12 1999)
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.): the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date 1 3 2001) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 12 1999)
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.): the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date 2 3 2001) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.): the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date 30 11 1999) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.): the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date 1 12 1999) (Date 30 6 1999) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The two version tables tile: the day Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) ends, the Rg 5 table begins.
#ASSERT `Rg 5: the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date 1 3 2001) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 5: the effective day of the version of the Regulations that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` (Date 2 3 2001) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2001)
-- Reg 2: a "station" is a transmitter, a receiver, a combination, or an accessory, used or intended to be used for radio-communication.
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the thing is a "station"` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the thing is a "station"` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 2: the thing is a "station"` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53A(4): the station is a "relevant radio-communication station"` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 53A(4): the station is a "relevant radio-communication station"` FALSE)
-- Reg 4(1): "Except as provided in the First Schedule, no person shall possess, establish, install or use any station in any place or on board any local vessel or aircraft or in any vehicle in Singapore unless he has a valid licence".
#ASSERT `Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 3 (1999 Ed.) reg 4(1): the person contravenes the regulation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
